Here is a plan for one day in Amsterdam for a visitor with interests in parks, gardens, and viewpoints:

```
{
  "stops": [
    {
      "name": "Westerpark",
      "start": "09:00",
      "end": "10:30"
    },
    {
      "name": "NEMO Science Center",
      "start": "11:00",
      "end": "12:30"
    },
    {
      "name": "Lunch at Café Papeneiland",
      "start": "13:00",
      "end": "14:30"
    },
    {
      "name": "Keukenhof Gardens (winter gardens)",
      "start": "15:00",
      "end": "17:00"
    },
    {
      "name": "EYE Film Museum",
      "start": "18:00",
      "end": "20:00"
    },
    {
      "name": "Leidseplein viewpoint",
      "start": "20:30",
      "end": "21:00"
    }
  ]
}
```

Note: I've assumed that the visitor wants to visit the winter gardens at Keukenhof, as the regular Keukenhof Gardens are closed during the winter months. If you'd like to visit the regular gardens, I can suggest an alternative stop. Also, please check the opening hours and walking times between each stop to ensure that the itinerary works for the visitor.
